    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0627" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/179a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-18T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Morris.</p>
                <p>Graves reports you have approved his withholding delivery of rifles because of
                    Kalmikoff incident. Graves admits Kalmikoff irresponsible. … This Government has
                    formally undertaken to aid Kolchak with munitions, food and supplies and made
                    rifle contract with Russian authorities here on that premise. Department feels
                    very strongly unless there are adequate reasons to the contrary that rifles
                    should be delivered in fulfilment of formal obligation and that <pb facs="0628"
                        n="516" xml:id="pg516"/> Kalmikoff incident should be regarded as
                    unwarranted action by unauthorized and irresponsible person, a matter which
                    should be taken up with Omsk Government separately. Please let Department have
                    your views at once.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d555-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d555-f1" n="66" xml:id="d555-f1-content">
                <p>Answered by Ambassador Morris in par. 6 of telegram of Sept. 23, 5 p.m., <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg432">p. 432</ref>.</p>
            </note>
